{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":55485,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"685553a3-d34a-5acb-8b25-a6a6348aeccb","total_cost_usd":0.503668,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10727,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5648,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10727,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5648,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":6628,"outputTokens":16,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.006708,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":5648,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10727,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.49696,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer_participant_id\": \"actor:dependence-free-batch-c-reviewer-fable-20\", \"reviews\": [{\"case_id\": \"case:41cfd59360a1ca24ca4b\", \"verdict\": \"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope\", \"bounded_statement\": null, \"root_cause\": null, \"issue_class\": null, \"evidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The workflow collapses the six repeated clearance runs per mussel to one pre-phase mean and one post-phase mean per animal before any statistical test is run, so each independent unit (mussel_id) contributes exactly one paired row to the inferential procedure.\", \"observed_value\": \"per_animal_table() computes np.mean over pre runs and post runs within each mussel\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 40, \"end_line\": 49, \"quoted_text\": \"def per_animal_table(order, runs):\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Collapse repeated runs to one pre mean and one post mean per animal.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    table = []\\n    for animal in order:\\n        pre_runs = runs[animal][\\\"pre\\\"]\\n        post_runs = runs[animal][\\\"post\\\"]\\n        if not pre_runs or not post_runs:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"mussel \\\" + animal + \\\" does not have both phases\\\")\\n        pre = float(np.mean(pre_runs))\\n        post = float(np.mean(post_runs))\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The paired t-test is applied to the 12 per-animal pre and post means (one entry per mussel), with n = 12 and df = 11, not to the 72 run-level rows.\", \"observed_value\": \"stats.ttest_rel applied to arrays of length 12 built from the collapsed per-animal table; df = n - 1 = 11\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 73, \"end_line\": 77, \"quoted_text\": \"    pre = np.array([row[\\\"pre\\\"] for row in table], dtype=float)\\n    post = np.array([row[\\\"post\\\"] for row in table], dtype=float)\\n    change = post - pre\\n    n = int(change.size)\\n    df = n - 1\"}, {\"path\": \"workflow/analysis.py\", \"start_line\": 86, \"end_line\": 86, \"quoted_text\": \"    tstat, pvalue = stats.ttest_rel(post, pre)\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The report's selected result states n = 12 mussels and t(11), matching an analysis at the level of the independent unit; recomputation from the raw run-level data confirms the reported per-animal means (e.g., MU-01 pre mean (3.16+3.49+3.55)/3 = 3.400) and the test statistic: the 12 within-animal changes have mean -0.9167 L/h, SD 0.2125, giving t = -0.9167/(0.2125/sqrt(12)) = -14.94 on 11 df, exactly as reported.\", \"observed_value\": \"reported t(11) = -14.944 reproduces from 12 independent within-animal changes\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 38, \"end_line\": 44, \"quoted_text\": \"- Independent units analysed: 12 mussels (72 clearance runs collapsed to 12 paired rows)\\n- Mean pre-exposure clearance: 3.383 L/h\\n- Mean post-exposure clearance: 2.467 L/h\\n- Mean within-animal change: -0.917 L/h (SD 0.212, 95% CI -1.052 to -0.782)\\n- Paired t-test: t(11) = -14.944, p < 0.0001\\n\\n[selected-result] Particle clearance fell after the 10-day warming exposure: mean within-animal change -0.917 L/h (95% CI -1.052 to -0.782), two-sided paired t(11) = -14.944, p < 0.0001, n = 12 mussels.\"}]}, {\"description\": \"The analysis section of the report accurately describes the aggregation to one analysed row per independent unit, consistent with the data description's requirement of a single summary per animal per phase.\", \"observed_value\": \"report describes averaging within animal and phase before testing\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"results/report.md\", \"start_line\": 13, \"end_line\": 17, \"quoted_text\": \"Clearance rates were averaged within animal and phase, which leaves one pre-exposure mean\\nand one post-exposure mean per mussel and therefore exactly one analysed row per\\nindependent unit (`mussel_id`). The 12 within-animal changes (post minus pre) were tested\\nagainst zero with a two-sided paired t-test (`scipy.stats.ttest_rel`); the 95% interval\\nuses the Student t quantile on 11 degrees of freedom.\"}, {\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 14, \"end_line\": 15, \"quoted_text\": \"One row is: a single clearance run on one tagged mussel on one measurement day\\nIndependent unit column: mussel_id\"}]}], \"counterevidence_atoms\": [{\"description\": \"The input data are in long format with each mussel appearing six times (72 rows from 12 animals), so the raw table does contain repeated entries of each independent unit; if these rows had been fed directly into a row-independent test the issue class would be present. This structural risk is the only element pointing toward the issue, and it is neutralized by the within-animal aggregation performed before testing.\", \"observed_value\": \"72 run-level rows, 6 per mussel_id, in data/input.csv\", \"source_spans\": [{\"path\": \"data-description.md\", \"start_line\": 11, \"end_line\": 12, \"quoted_text\": \"The file `data/input.csv` is stored in long format: the same mussel appears six times,\\nonce per clearance run.\"}, {\"path\": \"data/input.csv\", \"start_line\": 2, \"end_line\": 7, \"quoted_text\": \"MU-01,1,pre,0,62.4,15.0,3.16\\nMU-01,2,pre,2,62.4,14.9,3.49\\nMU-01,3,pre,4,62.4,15.1,3.55\\nMU-01,4,post,16,62.4,15.0,2.68\\nMU-01,5,post,18,62.4,15.0,2.29\\nMU-01,6,post,20,62.4,14.9,2.53\"}]}], \"falsification_attempt\": \"I tried to show the issue is present by checking whether run-level rows leak into the test despite the report's claims. First, I traced the code path: read_runs() groups the 72 rows by mussel_id and phase, per_animal_table() reduces each group to a single mean, and stats.ttest_rel receives only the length-12 pre and post arrays, so no run-level replicate reaches the test. Second, I checked the reported degrees of freedom against what a pseudoreplicated analysis would produce: a run-level paired test on 36 pre/post pairs (or 72 rows) would give df around 35 or 70, but the report states t(11), consistent only with 12 analysed units. Third, I recomputed the statistic from the raw CSV: the 12 within-animal changes (-0.900, -0.700, -1.200, -0.800, -1.000, -0.600, -1.100, -0.900, -1.300, -0.800, -1.000, -0.700) have mean -0.9167 and SD 0.2125, yielding t = -14.94 on 11 df, matching the reported value exactly; a run-level analysis would not reproduce this SD or t. All three checks failed to demonstrate the issue, so the conclusion as stated is supported by an analysis performed at the correct independent-unit level.\", \"cross_case_evidence_used\": false, \"unresolved_material_questions\": [], \"self_reported_confidence\": \"high\"}]}","ttft_ms":29928,"ttft_stream_ms":1495,"time_to_request_ms":22,"type":"result","duration_ms":56272,"uuid":"00b109fc-916d-4c05-b6c9-85602df55036"}
